  "worked_solution": "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nIn our case, the trajectory (solution) passes through the point $(x,y)=(1,-1)$ in the phase space. Substituting the coordinates of this point into the equations of our system, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{\u2032} & =5x-y \\\\  & =5(1)-(-1) \\\\  & =5+1 \\\\  & =6 \\\\ {y}^{\u2032} & =-x-2y \\\\  & =-1-2(-1) \\\\  & =-1+2 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent vector to the trajectory is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{\u2032} \\\\ {y}^{\u2032}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
